[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2789814698","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105192#issuecomment-2789814698","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105192","id":2789814698,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mSTGq","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-09T13:52:06Z","updated_at":"2025-04-09T13:52:06Z","body":"> I made an out-of-project benchmark for this, because I was interested in the performance difference. On my system (macOS arm64), non-recursive mutexes can apparently be 35% faster than recursive ones:\r\n\r\nTested on Linux with GCC 14.2.1, it seems to mostly have a significant difference in non-optimized builds. With `-O2` or `-O3` there's a difference but less than 10%.\r\n\r\n```\r\n~$ gcc --version\r\ngcc (GCC) 14.2.1 20250110 (Red Hat 14.2.1-7)\r\nCopyright (C) 2024 Free Software Foundation, Inc.\r\nThis is free software; see the source for copying conditions.  There is NO\r\nwarranty; not even for MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.\r\n~$ g++ -O0 test.cpp \r\n~$ ./a.out \r\n1687ms\r\n2172ms\r\n~$ ./a.out \r\n1690ms\r\n2144ms\r\n~$ ./a.out \r\n1688ms\r\n2157ms\r\n~$ g++ -O2 test.cpp \r\n~$ ./a.out \r\n557ms\r\n605ms\r\n~$ ./a.out \r\n543ms\r\n585ms\r\n~$ ./a.out \r\n539ms\r\n591ms\r\n~$ g++ -O3 test.cpp \r\n~$ ./a.out \r\n570ms\r\n586ms\r\n~$ ./a.out \r\n538ms\r\n585ms\r\n~$ ./a.out \r\n539ms\r\n590ms\r\n~$ g++ -O3 -flto test.cpp \r\n~$ ./a.out \r\n548ms\r\n594ms\r\n~$ ./a.out \r\n550ms\r\n579ms\r\n~$ ./a.out \r\n537ms\r\n587ms\r\n```\r\n\r\nI get similar numbers with clang (also using GCC libstdc++ so I guess that's expected).\r\nStill, ca. 10% performance improvement isn't bad.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2789814698/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2833727340","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105192#issuecomment-2833727340","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105192","id":2833727340,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6o5z9s","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/even